  ('saying-goodbye-well', 1, 'Take one slow breath and say quietly to yourself, "Something is changing, and that is okay."'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 2, 'Send a two line thank you text to someone who made this chapter kinder, naming one thing they did.'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 3, 'Stand in the doorway of a place you are leaving and look around slowly, as if seeing it for the first time.'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 4, 'Mark the end date on your calendar and add one word for how you hope to feel when it arrives.'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 5, 'Draw a line down the middle of a page, write this chapter on the left and the next on the right, and add one word to each side.'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 6, 'Write one sentence on a sticky note that names what is ending, then put it where you will see it.'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 7, 'Slip a brief thank you note onto the desk of a coworker who made your workdays easier.'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 8, 'Sit for ten quiet minutes in a favorite cafe and notice the sounds you will remember.'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 9, 'Brew a cup of tea this evening and raise it in a quiet toast to the place or person you are leaving.'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 10, 'Write down the names of three people you most want to keep in touch with once this chapter closes.'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 11, 'List three things that will be different once this chapter closes, using plain words and no judgment.'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 12, 'Tell your barista this morning that their friendly hello has been a bright spot in your routine.'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 13, 'Walk slowly through your home tonight and say goodbye to one room at a time.'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 14, 'Write a short letter to the chapter that is closing, then fold it and keep it somewhere safe.'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 15, 'Choose how you will reach each of those three people, whether a call, a letter or a voice note, and jot it beside their name.'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 16, 'Notice one feeling about the change while you brush your teeth tonight, and simply name it.'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 17, 'Note the names of the people you want to say goodbye to properly before this change happens.'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 18, 'Notice the smell of your home when you first walk in today, the scent you usually stop noticing after a minute.'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 19, 'Switch on a lamp at dusk and let it mark a few quiet minutes of thinking about what this time gave you.'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 20, 'Set a gentle reminder on your phone to check in with a friend who has moved, timed for an ordinary evening a few weeks out.'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 21, 'Jot down two feelings that are both true right now, like a little sad and a little excited.'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 22, 'Send a text to a neighbor asking if they have ten minutes for a goodbye chat on the porch this evening.'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 23, 'Choose one small memento from this place that fits in the palm of your hand.'),
  ('saying-goodbye-well', 24, 'Keep your usual wake up time this morning, even if the days ahead are full of boxes and farewells.'),
